## Lore

The Mokoloi are the Reptile Men of the Northlands: crocodile-like
humanoids with pale to dark green skin, a ridge down the spine, a thick
round muzzle full of teeth, small eyes on the sides of a long head and a
heavy tail that balances a broad, hunched upper body. They are aliens. On
their own drying, dying world a mage-priest found three thousand of her
people asleep in a buried cryogenic institute and spent her life on a
ritual that sent the whole building through a rift. It arrived in the
swamps of northern Australia in about 66 P.A.

Some fifteen thousand now live in two swamp cities of stone buildings,
canals and pyramids. They still worship their lost homeworld as a god and
argue over why they were sent here: as a reward, as a test, or to take a
new home by right. They trust magic over machines, building an alien
Techno-Wizardry and a Stone Magic they will share with nobody. Society is
an oligarchy of councils and mildly matriarchal: females hold most
positions of rule, scholarship and magic, while males lean to exploration
and war. Disputes are settled by combat or contest, and those who become a
burden are expected to walk into the wild and not return.

They are quick tempered, aggressive, bold and supremacist, and they hold
mammals in low esteem. A debt, though, is honored: a Mokoloi will befriend
anyone it owes until the debt is repaid, and then simply leave.

## GM Notes

The book heads the Mokoloi an NPC villain and optional player race.

Choose the male or female variant. Males fight with Mokoloi Martial Arts
(+2 initiative and +3 pull punch are applied; +1 attack with the tail, +1
attack underwater and +2 to dodge underwater are not) and are +3 to save vs
Horror Factor; females fight as Hand to Hand: Expert and are +4. The
Mokoloi Martial Arts damage table and the roll-over attack are listed under
the natural abilities.

Vulnerability: dry heat. Without full immersion in water every other day a
Mokoloi is -2 to dodge, parry and initiative and loses one M.D.C. a day.

Size 6-7 feet (1.8 to 2.1 m) standing, 12-15 feet (3.6 to 4.6 m) long
lying prone or swimming, tail included. Weight 250 + 6D10 lb. Life span 45
years, some to 70. About 45% are female. Habitat is swampy wetland, so far
mainly the Northland.

Mokoloi Techno-Wizard gear in the catalog, for a G.M. who equips one: the
Constrictor Web Gun (mokoloi-constrictor-web-gun), Knuckle Dusters
(mokoloi-knuckle-dusters), Chatra Lava Gun (mokoloi-chatra-lava-gun),
Warrior''s Blade (mokoloi-warriors-blade) and Snake Back armor
(mokoloi-snake-back-armor). The race block grants no starting equipment
and no money. About 12-15% of females hold Stone Magic; roughly 5% of
males and another 10% of females are Ley Line Walkers, mostly of level
1D4+2.

They are unsure whom to trust. The Horune Pirates, fellow non-mammals, are
fledgling allies and trading partners. The Aboriginal tribes worry them,
the Tech-Cities are current enemies, and they regard the supernatural,
vampires and demons above all, as natural enemies.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'mokoloi');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'mokoloi';

